        "original_id": "0948c983-8c74-5554-8b94-a9f8781b3953",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Reno–Tahoe International Airport, downtown Reno, Washoe County, Nevada, Las Vegas, Lake Tahoe\n- Organizations: United States Army\n- People: Jesse L. Reno\n- Roles: Union General, United States Army officer\n- Topics: airport identifiers, airport activity ranking, military service\n\nFacts:\n- Jesse Lee Reno was born on April 20, 1823, and died on September 14, 1862.\n- Jesse L. Reno was a career United States Army officer who served in the Mexican–American War, the Utah War, on the western frontier, and as a Union General during the American Civil War.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport is named after Jesse L. Reno and Lake Tahoe.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport is a public and military use airport located three nautical miles southeast of downtown Reno in Washoe County, Nevada.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport has the identifiers IATA RNO, ICAO KRNO, and FAA LID RNO.\n- Reno–Tahoe International Airport is Nevada's second busiest commercial airport after McCarran International Airport in Las Vegas.",
